BIBLE STUDY • LESSON 01
</div>

<h1>
Why Study the Bible?
</h1>

<p>
Understanding why Scripture matters
and how studying God's Word can shape
our faith, thinking and daily lives.
</p>

</div>

</section>


<!-- LESSON -->

<main class="lesson-content">

<div class="container">


<h2>
Introduction
</h2>

<p>
The Bible is central to the Christian faith.
It contains Scripture that teaches about God,
humanity, faith, wisdom, salvation and
how believers are called to live.
</p>

<p>
Studying the Bible is more than simply reading
words on a page. It involves seeking to understand
the message of Scripture and considering how
its teachings apply to our lives.
</p>


<div class="scripture">

<p>
"All Scripture is God-breathed and is useful
for teaching, rebuking, correcting and training
in righteousness."
</p>

<strong>
2 Timothy 3:16
</strong>

</div>


<h2>
1. To Know God
</h2>

<p>
The Bible helps us learn about God's character,
His works and His relationship with humanity.
Through Scripture, Christians seek to understand
who God is and what He desires.
</p>


<h2>
2. To Grow in Wisdom
</h2>

<p>
Scripture contains teachings that encourage
wisdom, discipline, humility, love and
understanding.
</p>

<div class="scripture">

<p>
"If any of you lacks wisdom, you should ask God,
who gives generously to all without finding fault,
and it will be given to you."
</p>

<strong>
James 1:5
</strong>

</div>


<h2>
3. To Strengthen Faith
</h2>

<p>
Regular engagement with Scripture can help
believers reflect on God's promises and develop
a deeper understanding of faith.
</p>

<div class="scripture">

<p>
"So faith comes from hearing,
and hearing through the word of Christ."
</p>

<strong>
Romans 10:17
</strong>

</div>


<h2>
4. To Guide Our Lives
</h2>

<p>
The Bible provides principles that can help
people think about their choices, relationships,
character and responsibilities.
</p>

<div class="scripture">

<p>
"Your word is a lamp for my feet,
a light on my path."
</p>

<strong>
Psalm 119:105
</strong>

</div>


<h2>
How Should We Study the Bible?
</h2>

<p>
A useful approach is to slow down, read the
passage carefully, consider its context,
identify what it teaches and reflect on
how the message should influence our lives.
</p>

<ul>

<li>
Read the passage carefully.
</li>

<li>
Consider the context.
</li>

<li>
Identify the main message.
</li>

<li>
Compare related Scripture where appropriate.
</li>

<li>
Reflect on how the lesson applies to life.
</li>

<li>
Pray for wisdom and understanding.
</li>

</ul>


